{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers","id":1463768,"title":"Cryptkeepers -- A Splat for Storytellers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-13T18:32:28-07:00","id":1463768,"title":"Cryptkeepers -- A Splat for Storytellers?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">I've heard many people ask about any other potential splats which may be developed for the &quot;Chronicles of Darkness&quot; and one popped into my head while going over old horror anthology shows and films:<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Mortuary Collection\u201d \u2013 2021<br /> \u201cCreepshow\u201d \u2013 all iterations<br /> \u201cTales From the Hood\u201d \u2013 1995<br /> \u201cTales From the Crypt\u201d tv series \u2013 1990\u2019s<br /> John Carpenter\u2019s \u201cBody Bags\u201d \u2013 1993<br /> \u201cTales From the Crypt\u201d \u2013 1972<br /> \u201cNight Gallery\u201d \u2013 1969-1973<br /> \u201cDr. Terror\u2019s House of Horrors\u201d \u2013 1965 </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Each one centered on a mysterious, apparently supernatural host relaying stories from a collection they possess; sometimes from objects from various people or, more often than not, from dead people they have access to. Also, they seem to tell stories which relay a sort of karmic theme for many of the characters. I started to wonder, could there be a splat for the storytellers themselves? Let the storytellers be a character in their own chronicles? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A splat for &quot;Cryptkeepers&quot; as it were--strange supernatural beings who, for one reason or another, are cursed to collect and share stories from the Chronicles of Darkness--not able to interfere directly, but able to influence events to flow from a specific karmic theme. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-13T19:02:07-07:00","id":1463772,"title":"","content":"The idea isn't half bad, but you would have to present something to make it interesting for protagonists. What this game would be about for the players? Or is it meant also literally for NPCs?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T05:25:51-07:00","id":1463819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1463772#post1463772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea isn't half bad, but you would have to present something to make it interesting for protagonists. What this game would be about for the players? Or is it meant also literally for NPCs?</div> </div> </div> </div>About making amends perhaps? I don't know, I'm just throwing an idea out here to see if it would have any merit--In &quot;The Mortuary Collection&quot; (2021) you have a funeral director relaying stories from the bodies in his morgue, only to find out in the end that he's a cursed individual who not only can't die but also can't leave the Mortuary. <br /> <br /> Perhaps these hosts are people who were terrible people in life and are now cursed in death to not only collect stories but also influence stories that ensure the wicked are punished for their crimes. <br /> <br /> Mechanically it would allow the storytellers to interact with their players in a more direct way, being a character in their own chronicle whom the other players can interact with whether they are playing Vampire, Werewolf, Deviant, etc. It could maybe include NPCs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T07:43:04-07:00","id":1463825,"title":"","content":"I do think they have a lot of potential as an NPC oriented type of creature, I'm just not sure if it qualifies as a &quot;splat&quot;. But it is surely a worthy idea that I'll at leas ruminate for use n my own chronicles, even if I can't find actual further ideas to throw here.<br /> <br /> The concept works well as a cross-splat phenomenon. Anyone could become a Crypt Keeper for a number of reasons, but the role is so archetypal that it carries a weight all its own to add to the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T14:47:46-07:00","id":1463887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1463825#post1463825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do think they have a lot of potential as an NPC oriented type of creature, I'm just not sure if it qualifies as a &quot;splat&quot;. But it is surely a worthy idea that I'll at leas ruminate for use n my own chronicles, even if I can't find actual further ideas to throw here.<br /> <br /> The concept works well as a cross-splat phenomenon. Anyone could become a Crypt Keeper for a number of reasons, but the role is so archetypal that it carries a weight all its own to add to the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, maybe they don't really work as an official splat, but maybe an alternate idea for how storytellers could work with players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-14T21:35:33-07:00","id":1463948,"title":"","content":"A Cryptkeeper splat would be interesting, though it would take some altering and expanding of the base idea to make it a group of Cryptkeepers work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T09:56:55-07:00","id":1464047,"title":"","content":"So wait, something like the Ryuujin from Ryuutama?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T11:16:11-07:00","id":1464059,"title":"","content":"I am joining in because this sounds like a gameline in the making *eyes with interest*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T12:40:31-07:00","id":1464066,"title":"","content":"It's literally main idea about <b>They Came From Beyond the Grave!</b>, game having premiere in coming weeks. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T15:30:00-07:00","id":1464094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1464059#post1464059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am joining in because this sounds like a gameline in the making *eyes with interest*</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure it's a <i>gameline</i>, per se, but the notion has functional space for a sourcebook, or at least part of one.<br /> <br /> And I'm not going to be the one to shoot down the notion of playing the manifested superego of a psychic rabbit detective mutated into a gigantic beast by a toybox filled with powerful toys from another dimension.<br /> <br /> EDIT: or the writer writing out their own departure and return, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-15-2021, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-15T19:00:19-07:00","id":1464126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1464047#post1464047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wait, something like the Ryuujin from Ryuutama?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure, I'm not familiar with that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1463948#post1463948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Cryptkeeper splat would be interesting, though it would take some altering and expanding of the base idea to make it a group of Cryptkeepers work.</div> </div> </div> </div>True that -- it would be a splat, or just a character npc set which could work with all other splats, and support players in their chronicles. Not interfering directly, but rather influencing events.<br /> <br /> Like perhaps they're beings who died and on the other side, instead of being banished to Hell, they were given a chance to help the world and learn from it in a way they didn't have a chance to in their own life. Maybe they relay a 'dream-vision' to a player(s) about an event that will happen in the future like in &quot;Dr. Terror's House of Horrors,&quot; while another time they may show a story to a victim about the horrors done by someone they know (and plans to do to the victim next), and other times they just tell a story about someone else to confer a lesson about comeuppance like in &quot;Tales From the Crypt&quot; as a framing device for the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T13:44:42-07:00","id":1465689,"title":"","content":"If we put the focus more on spooky items, then we would have a solid core gameplay loop. What if being the creepy host with a massive collection of items was the endgame and the Cryptkeeper's usual activities consisted of tracking down supernatural items to add to their collection. We could take a page from Deviant and have the Cryptkeeper's power stat only go to 5, with the power they've invested in any given item accounting for the rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25732-wrecksalot","name":"wrecksalot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T18:24:20-07:00","id":1465733,"title":"","content":"That could work very well! Would probably need maybe some expanded item creation rules though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T23:28:35-07:00","id":1466096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wrecksalot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1465689#post1465689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we put the focus more on spooky items, then we would have a solid core gameplay loop. What if being the creepy host with a massive collection of items was the endgame and the Cryptkeeper's usual activities consisted of tracking down supernatural items to add to their collection. We could take a page from Deviant and have the Cryptkeeper's power stat only go to 5, with the power they've invested in any given item accounting for the rest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea, but to what purpose do they collect these items which could also be expressed in gameplay?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T09:02:56-07:00","id":1466133,"title":"","content":"Instead of collecting items, I think it could be that they collect stories, and maybe they create items from those stories. Like empowering a trinket that was tangentially involved with the energy of the entire story.<br /> <br /> They could make it in several steps. They first investigate to piece the story together, then they build the narrative, and finally they pass the story along. Each step empowers the new item in some way.<br /> <br /> About what to do with that, different Z-Splats may have different reasons/goals with the items and/or the stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-01T15:37:57-07:00","id":1466182,"title":"","content":"Looks like a new type of Immortals with a focus on Vestiges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T08:09:56-07:00","id":1466288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1466096#post1466096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting idea, but to what purpose do they collect these items which could also be expressed in gameplay?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking that they would serve as, like disciplines or variations. You only get the most barebones effect out of it when you get it, but you can empower them through xp","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25732-wrecksalot","name":"wrecksalot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T20:20:57-07:00","id":1466868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wrecksalot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1466288#post1466288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking that they would serve as, like disciplines or variations. You only get the most barebones effect out of it when you get it, but you can empower them through xp</div> </div> </div> </div>Would that work better as a kind of NPC, or would it work as a game splat in your opinion? I honestly don't know, I've just been throwing ideas out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-05T21:17:30-07:00","id":1466891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1466868#post1466868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would that work better as a kind of NPC, or would it work as a game splat in your opinion? I honestly don't know, I've just been throwing ideas out there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think if we work enough on how this character collects stories and craft narratives, we can have a suitable Player Splat.<br /> <br /> A staple of the Gothic Horror that we still work little in RPGs is the Witness Protagonist. In the source literature the protagonist of the story is less one of the villains or heroes, and more someone simply witnessing the story unfold from a third person perspective.<br /> <br /> This is all over the place there, from the original Castle of Otranto to the humor of Scooby-Doo (that despite all its goofiness is <i>extremely</i> loyal to Gothic tropes).<br /> <br /> For our more familiar supernatural horror, an excellent example is the book <i>Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde</i>. The original novella's protagonist is Gabriel John Utterson, Jekyll's lawyer, who investigates his client's weird business with the shady figure of Hyde, a man obviously up to no good and seemingly engaged in blackmail against the good doctor Henry Jekyll.<br /> <br /> So the entire story develops as Utterson investigates, interrogates people, collects documents and evidence, and at some point even breaks into Jekyll's house after the truth. But while he's the protagonist and the one driving the action, the story isn't his, but the narrative that emerges from his findings about the conflict between Jekyll and Hyde, until the nature of their relationship truly emerges.<br /> <br /> Capturing this most elusive aspect of the Gothic genre into an RPG would be a worth endeavor in making this splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T04:06:58-08:00","id":1467336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1466891#post1466891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think if we work enough on how this character collects stories and craft narratives, we can have a suitable Player Splat.<br /> <br /> A staple of the Gothic Horror that we still work little in RPGs is the Witness Protagonist. In the source literature the protagonist of the story is less one of the villains or heroes, and more someone simply witnessing the story unfold from a third person perspective.<br /> <br /> This is all over the place there, from the original Castle of Otranto to the humor of Scooby-Doo (that despite all its goofiness is <i>extremely</i> loyal to Gothic tropes).<br /> <br /> For our more familiar supernatural horror, an excellent example is the book <i>Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde</i>. The original novella's protagonist is Gabriel John Utterson, Jekyll's lawyer, who investigates his client's weird business with the shady figure of Hyde, a man obviously up to no good and seemingly engaged in blackmail against the good doctor Henry Jekyll.<br /> <br /> So the entire story develops as Utterson investigates, interrogates people, collects documents and evidence, and at some point even breaks into Jekyll's house after the truth. But while he's the protagonist and the one driving the action, the story isn't his, but the narrative that emerges from his findings about the conflict between Jekyll and Hyde, until the nature of their relationship truly emerges.<br /> <br /> Capturing this most elusive aspect of the Gothic genre into an RPG would be a worth endeavor in making this splat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, here's an idea, Cryptkeepers have a special connection to their Crypts, similar to a Beast's lair. It not only houses all the items and stories they collected, but also contains their essence in a way. <br /> <br /> The Crypt is also ephemeral, moving about--disappearing and reappearing--where the Cryptkeeper deems it necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T15:37:18-08:00","id":1467387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1467336#post1467336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, here's an idea, Cryptkeepers have a special connection to their Crypts, similar to a Beast's lair. It not only houses all the items and stories they collected, but also contains their essence in a way.<br /> <br /> The Crypt is also ephemeral, moving about--disappearing and reappearing--where the Cryptkeeper deems it necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good one, but maybe the Crypt is greater than the Keeper?<br /> <br /> It reminds me of a pair of such storytellers from DC Comics, Cain and Abel and their House of Mystery and House of Secrets. The two Houses are also independent entities in their own right and on occasion hold other inhabitants while never exactly &quot;serving&quot; no one.<br /> <br /> You don't own them in any sense just because you reside there, although they may give you some control over their state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-12T15:39:46-08:00","id":1467605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1467387#post1467387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a good one, but maybe the Crypt is greater than the Keeper?<br /> <br /> It reminds me of a pair of such storytellers from DC Comics, Cain and Abel and their House of Mystery and House of Secrets. The two Houses are also independent entities in their own right and on occasion hold other inhabitants while never exactly &quot;serving&quot; no one.<br /> <br /> You don't own them in any sense just because you reside there, although they may give you some control over their state.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The Mortuary Collection&quot; established such an idea -- the mortuary trades hands between one person to another; the storyteller sells it to a serial murderer so she is entrapped there while the previous owner is allowed to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-13T20:58:59-08:00","id":1467758,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Cryptkeepers were people chosen by these sentient places, these &quot;Crypts&quot;. These &quot;crypts&quot; pluck lost souls from outer darkness so that they may help feed them certain karmic energies for a certain length of time. In return, the soul is given a chance to escape their fate and perhaps get a second chance. <br /> <br /> Which would explain why these characters are always so grimly giddy--despite all the macabre happenings around them, they are getting a free ticket out of Hell, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T03:11:48-08:00","id":1468109,"title":"","content":"What would you picture their powers to be? <br /> <br /> Some part of me believes they could manifest many things within their respective Crypts (as seen with HBO's Cryptkeeper always seemingly doing something comically grim with any number of props or people) but be much more limited outside of their crypts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-17T06:14:35-08:00","id":1468122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468109#post1468109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you picture their powers to be?<br /> <br /> Some part of me believes they could manifest many things within their respective Crypts (as seen with HBO's Cryptkeeper always seemingly doing something comically grim with any number of props or people) but be much more limited outside of their crypts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends a lot on how we want to play them out.<br /> <br /> One aspect of the splat should certainly be the hosting of a storytelling. While Beasts have Heroes fated to search them for a climatic battle, AFAIK, Keepers should receive Seekers, people that come to the Crypt in search of something, knowingly or not, either an object or an information, to be delivered along with the moral of the story behind it.<br /> <br /> But that is just the Keeper dealing with Seekers. We also need to define how the Keepers collect the stories in the first place, and then we should define the skills they develop for going out there. Of course, those can be relatively mild abilities, as their main goal is to collect narratives and not to resolve them <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe their standard powers should be subtle, geared towards survival, travel and acquiring information. Then there are the powers they derive from the stories they collect, in the form of tales and nick knacks.<br /> <br /> I also think they should be able to bring the power of the stories to the outside world under certain circumstances, like when asked for a Seeker or after telling the relevant story to their victims-to-be. They have a connection to the Crypts, but their power is in the storytelling itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T15:31:12-08:00","id":1468431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468122#post1468122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That depends a lot on how we want to play them out.<br /> <br /> One aspect of the splat should certainly be the hosting of a storytelling. While Beasts have Heroes fated to search them for a climatic battle, AFAIK, Keepers should receive Seekers, people that come to the Crypt in search of something, knowingly or not, either an object or an information, to be delivered along with the moral of the story behind it.<br /> <br /> But that is just the Keeper dealing with Seekers. We also need to define how the Keepers collect the stories in the first place, and then we should define the skills they develop for going out there. Of course, those can be relatively mild abilities, as their main goal is to collect narratives and not to resolve them <i>per se</i>.<br /> <br /> Maybe their standard powers should be subtle, geared towards survival, travel and acquiring information. Then there are the powers they derive from the stories they collect, in the form of tales and nick knacks.<br /> <br /> I also think they should be able to bring the power of the stories to the outside world under certain circumstances, like when asked for a Seeker or after telling the relevant story to their victims-to-be. They have a connection to the Crypts, but their power is in the storytelling itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should their powers have a theme of influencing the flow of events?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T16:18:41-08:00","id":1468436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468431#post1468431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should their powers have a theme of influencing the flow of events?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thinking about it, maybe not their powers, but their mere presence.<br /> <br /> As Gothic storytellers they shouldn't have the power to control the stories that unfold around them, but certainly be drawn to them. One option is that they have some effect in their surrounds that naturally &quot;raise the drama&quot; in the area.<br /> <br /> Fate distorts around them, thoughts and emotions seek closure, the <i>status quo</i> starts to crumble under the unnaturally increased weight of consequences in hold and debts owed. If the Keeper don't find a story, a story will find the Keeper through whatever actors are at hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T16:54:29-08:00","id":1468437,"title":"","content":"This is starting to sound like a midpoint between Mummy and Beast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-20T18:02:32-08:00","id":1468443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468437#post1468437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is starting to sound like a midpoint between Mummy and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this good or bad?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T07:44:34-08:00","id":1468499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1464126#post1464126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not sure, I'm not familiar with (Ryuujin and Ryuutama)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ryuutama is a rules-light &quot;natural fantasy&quot; RPG set in a world where people randomly get wanderlust and go out to see the world. Traveling parties are secretly followed or accompanied by shapeshifting dragon NPCs (Ryuujin) controlled by the GM, writing travelogues of the group's exploits. They have their own stats and story-influencing abilities, which can help or hinder the party to make the journey more interesting. The travelogues are then fed to the Seasonal Dragons who created the world, who each have an affinity for particular story types. The Ryuujin has to spend their life force to activate their abilities and can die if, say, they undo a character death because they got attached to the group.<br /> So, I'm thinking the suggestion was something along the lines of:<br /> Cryptkeeper: &quot;This was when he realized his mistake...&quot; and the Cryptkeeper spending resources to force a Dramatic Failure or the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:23:49-08:00","id":1468564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BronzeDog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468499#post1468499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ryuutama is a rules-light &quot;natural fantasy&quot; RPG set in a world where people randomly get wanderlust and go out to see the world. Traveling parties are secretly followed or accompanied by shapeshifting dragon NPCs (Ryuujin) controlled by the GM, writing travelogues of the group's exploits. They have their own stats and story-influencing abilities, which can help or hinder the party to make the journey more interesting. The travelogues are then fed to the Seasonal Dragons who created the world, who each have an affinity for particular story types. The Ryuujin has to spend their life force to activate their abilities and can die if, say, they undo a character death because they got attached to the group.<br /> So, I'm thinking the suggestion was something along the lines of:<br /> Cryptkeeper: &quot;This was when he realized his mistake...&quot; and the Cryptkeeper spending resources to force a Dramatic Failure or the like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:25:39-08:00","id":1468565,"title":"","content":"Should the Cryptkeepers powers have a sort of karmic theme? <br /> <br /> Most of these series shows and comics seemed to run with the idea of the horrible things in these stories happening to people as a strange kind of comeuppance or poetic justice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:38:26-08:00","id":1468567,"title":"","content":"That could be interesting. Theirs powers could for example be more effective depending on karma. A power that curses a target could be easier if that target has done something bad perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T09:33:06-08:00","id":1468600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468565#post1468565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should the Cryptkeepers powers have a sort of karmic theme?<br /> <br /> Most of these series shows and comics seemed to run with the idea of the horrible things in these stories happening to people as a strange kind of comeuppance or poetic justice.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is Gothic Storytelling 101, which is the base genre for those stories.<br /> <br /> So pretty much. All their shtick revolves around warning tales and moral of the story. Imprudence begets catastrophe and evil is self-punishing.<br /> <br /> I don't think it should be in terms of strength, though, but triggers. When their target do X, Y happens.<br /> <br /> An important part of the genre is that the tales are about the consequences of the actions, not divine punishment, and choice matters a lot. Redemption is possible, but the Gothic villains suffer because they systematically chose the easy and/or convenient evil.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, I think their powers should always focus on the idea of choice, and have an appropriate escape clause where the victim escapes by making a sensible choice.<br /> <br /> Past is a predictor, not a cause. You can always expect people to conform to their past patterns, and the genre heavily implies this continuation. Even when the punishment comes from the past, it comes true because the target is unrepentant.<br /> <br /> But then, maybe some powers do play on the idea of behavioral patterns to induce targets into acting in a certain way, but it should be subtle and feel like natural choice instead of external control. Tempting is certainly an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-26T21:56:49-08:00","id":1468941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1468600#post1468600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is Gothic Storytelling 101, which is the base genre for those stories.<br /> <br /> So pretty much. All their shtick revolves around warning tales and moral of the story. Imprudence begets catastrophe and evil is self-punishing.<br /> <br /> I don't think it should be in terms of strength, though, but triggers. When their target do X, Y happens.<br /> <br /> An important part of the genre is that the tales are about the consequences of the actions, not divine punishment, and choice matters a lot. Redemption is possible, but the Gothic villains suffer because they systematically chose the easy and/or convenient evil.<br /> <br /> With this in mind, I think their powers should always focus on the idea of choice, and have an appropriate escape clause where the victim escapes by making a sensible choice.<br /> <br /> Past is a predictor, not a cause. You can always expect people to conform to their past patterns, and the genre heavily implies this continuation. Even when the punishment comes from the past, it comes true because the target is unrepentant.<br /> <br /> But then, maybe some powers do play on the idea of behavioral patterns to induce targets into acting in a certain way, but it should be subtle and feel like natural choice instead of external control. Tempting is certainly an option.</div> </div> </div> </div>So in a weird way their powers could work similarly a changeling's oaths--but instead of working with one's words and fate, it works with someone's choice and free will, and the outcomes therein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T11:54:21-08:00","id":1469264,"title":"","content":"What would the theme of the game be? Redemption?<br /> <br /> I guess it could revolve around learning how to make better choices. Who would be there antagonists though?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T03:06:57-08:00","id":1469297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greetings1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1469264#post1469264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the theme of the game be? Redemption?<br /> <br /> I guess it could revolve around learning how to make better choices. Who would be there antagonists though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking cycles, I think. At the core those stories usually have a character that will suffer the consequences for their cycles of behavior and self-justification. And that's common for the characters in the stories, the Seekers and the Keepers, at least that's my impression.<br /> <br /> That include redemption and making better choices, but also condemnation and learning lessons through others. If you don't break the cycle, the cycle breaks you. One way or another it stops... for you, at least. The stories of the Keeper give you an alternative before it's your time to become a story. And the Keeper may have also their own cycles to break.<br /> <br /> If we go this route, the antagonist should be a force of repetition, something that encourages people to form circular patterns of thought and action. For example, <i>to have love I need to protect &gt; to protect I need to be strong &gt; to be strong I need to control everything &gt; to control everything I need to be ruthless &gt; being ruthless means being feared and hated &gt; Fear and hate destroy love</i>. This is a very simple, and frighteningly common cycle, IRL already a lot of people follow this to some extent.<br /> <br /> Also, pride is probably a key factor, one of the most powerful forms of pride, the refuse to acknowledge one's premises are wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-02T18:12:55-08:00","id":1469452,"title":"","content":"That could work very well for Cryptkeepers. Hmm, maybe this Repetition force is connected to the them in a way, like Strix and vampires are perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-05T08:38:55-08:00","id":1469648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMrMultiverse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1463768-cryptkeepers-a-splat-for-storytellers?p=1469452#post1469452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could work very well for Cryptkeepers. Hmm, maybe this Repetition force is connected to the them in a way, like Strix and vampires are perhaps?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps they're a kind of lost soul that's jealous/enraged that the Cryptkeepers got a second chance and they didn't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T11:30:26-08:00","id":1470227,"title":"","content":"What would their sustenance be? What kind of ephemeral matter/energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26940-greetings1","name":"Greetings1","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-11T21:52:03-08:00","id":1470257,"title":"","content":"Perhaps, maybe their sustenance is from continuing/ending a story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27083-truemrmultiverse","name":"TrueMrMultiverse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27083_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-12T18:25:34-08:00","id":1470320,"title":"","content":"I think it is something in the stories. I'm struggling to name it, but they acquire it when they collect stories, and maybe again in a minor way when they retell those stories. It's something tied to story and storytelling as concepts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"m